Package: lxb-compositor
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Piotr Lewandowski <piotr.petexiness@gmail.com>
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Depends: @SHLIB_DEPENDS@, dbus, libwayland-client0, libwayland-server0,
 libwayland-egl1, libegl1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxcb1, libxcursor1,
 libxi6, libxkbcommon-x11-0
Recommends: seatd, xwayland, libgl1-mesa-dri
Suggests: mesa-vulkan-drivers
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/Petexy/LineXinBar
Description: Wayland compositor for LineXinBar, usable on its own
 A small DRM/KMS Wayland compositor that manages every connected display as an
 independent output, with per-output colour management, HDR and a night light.
 .
 This package is the compositor alone: it runs whatever client it is pointed
 at and assumes nothing about LineXinBar's own shell. That is what lets a
 display manager depend on it to put a login screen on the hardware without
 installing a desktop. Install lxb-desktop for the desktop itself.
